<article class="env-warning" id="054A">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/054A">Warning <span data-tag="054A">3.5.6.7</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Kan complex. We have now assigned two different meanings to the notation $\pi _{\leq 1}(X)$: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The fundamental groupoid of $X$ (Definition <a data-tag="00HZ" href="/tag/00HZ">1.4.6.12</a>), which is a category. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The fundamental $1$-groupoid of $X$ (Notation <a data-tag="0549" href="/tag/0549">3.5.6.6</a>), which is a simplicial set. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> However, the danger of confusion is slight: by virtue of Example <a data-tag="0546" href="/tag/0546">3.5.6.3</a>, the fundamental $1$-groupoid of $X$ is isomorphic to the nerve of the fundamental groupoid of $X$. </p>
</article>
